(5981252, 874571, 91716, '<td valign="top">That is such a cool photo, very original</td>', 'That is such a cool photo, very original', '2010-04-30 16:09:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981276, 874740, 67258, '<td valign="top">This is certainly well inside my personal top 10 of the challenge.  Given this is an advanced editing challenge, for me the photo would benefit with the white of the eyes being brightened/or whitened, and the piercing hole cloned from the ear lobe.  Nonetheless, one of the stronger entries.</td>', 'This is certainly well inside my personal top 10 of the challenge.  Given this is an advanced editing challenge, for me the photo would benefit with the white of the eyes being brightened/or whitened, and the piercing hole cloned from the ear lobe.  Nonetheless, one of the stronger entries.', '2010-04-30 16:34:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981280, 872953, 67258, '<td valign="top">I really like the composition, and the sense of ''action''.  Less keen on the off-white background, which is given a slightly mucky feel by the white of the shirt.  Also sems a tad over-sharpened.  Still, and 8 from me.</td>', 'I really like the composition, and the sense of ''action''.  Less keen on the off-white background, which is given a slightly mucky feel by the white of the shirt.  Also sems a tad over-sharpened.  Still, and 8 from me.', '2010-04-30 16:36:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981282, 875112, 67258, '<td valign="top">Superb use of depth of field and the bokeh qualities of your lens.</td>', 'Superb use of depth of field and the bokeh qualities of your lens.', '2010-04-30 16:37:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981307, 874920, 97166, '<td valign="top">I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score: <br/> <br/>I like the decision to focus more on what the model is wearing, other than the model itself. I''d considered a similar approach, but chickened out in the end. However, the focus, as I see it, seems to be a bit missed in this photo. Or, more specifically, the sharpness (it may not be a focus issue at all). There just doesn''t seem to be enough detail in the texture, and the shot loses some of the ipact because of this.</td>', 'I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score:  I like the decision to focus more on what the model is wearing, other than the model itself. I''d considered a similar approach, but chickened out in the end. However, the focus, as I see it, seems to be a bit missed in this photo. Or, more specifically, the sharpness (it may not be a focus issue at all). There just doesn''t seem to be enough detail in the texture, and the shot loses some of the ipact because of this.', '2010-04-30 17:00:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981309, 874715, 97166, '<td valign="top">I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score: <br/> <br/>Well, I can''t say that it''s not about fashion, but the over-use of whatever smoothing you chose to use takes away from the impact of this photo, for me. Loss of detail in the hair and boa, for one.  It also seems to be more intent on showing us a portrait, rather than a focus ON the fashion, if you understand where I''m trying to go.</td>', 'I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score:  Well, I can''t say that it''s not about fashion, but the over-use of whatever smoothing you chose to use takes away from the impact of this photo, for me. Loss of detail in the hair and boa, for one.  It also seems to be more intent on showing us a portrait, rather than a focus ON the fashion, if you understand where I''m trying to go.', '2010-04-30 17:02:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981311, 874655, 97166, '<td valign="top">I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score: <br/> <br/>Some harsher lighting, and a lack of sharpness and detail, render this photo from a top performer, to a low-middle pack effort, in my mind.  It''s unique and humorous. Edgy in its own way, but simply lacks the technical reach to put it above.</td>', 'I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score:  Some harsher lighting, and a lack of sharpness and detail, render this photo from a top performer, to a low-middle pack effort, in my mind.  It''s unique and humorous. Edgy in its own way, but simply lacks the technical reach to put it above.', '2010-04-30 17:03:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981315, 875013, 97166, '<td valign="top">I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score: <br/> <br/>For my part, I''m not really sure what part of "fashion" this photo is trying to tell me.  When I first look at it, I think "Holiday Decoration".  It simply doesn''t have a strong enough connection for me.</td>', 'I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score:  For my part, I''m not really sure what part of "fashion" this photo is trying to tell me.  When I first look at it, I think "Holiday Decoration".  It simply doesn''t have a strong enough connection for me.', '2010-04-30 17:04:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981319, 874519, 97166, '<td valign="top">I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score: <br/> <br/>I''m a sucker for purple.  A nicely done studio shot, but something in the model''s look seems a little forced to me. It lacks, in my eyes, JUST that amount of emotion needed to really grip me.  However, of course, DPC doesn''t really look for that. I''d imagine this is doing fairly well.</td>', 'I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score:  I''m a sucker for purple.  A nicely done studio shot, but something in the model''s look seems a little forced to me. It lacks, in my eyes, JUST that amount of emotion needed to really grip me.  However, of course, DPC doesn''t really look for that. I''d imagine this is doing fairly well.', '2010-04-30 17:05:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981320, 874871, 97166, '<td valign="top">I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score: <br/> <br/>Edgy, moody, and I like the connection to the viewer we''re being given here.  Very nicely lit and photographed.</td>', 'I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score:  Edgy, moody, and I like the connection to the viewer we''re being given here.  Very nicely lit and photographed.', '2010-04-30 17:06:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5981322, 873705, 97166, '<td valign="top">I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score: <br/> <br/>One of the better product shots I''ve seen so far.  The reliance on ''water drop'' to boost a generic offering, however, is really getting old for me. Sadly, that''s my own peeve, as I''m sure it''s going nowhere.</td>', 'I''ve decided to comment on every shot in this challenge, since I''m sitting at 1 comments, and I''d rather try and take a positive approach to this rather than simply whining about my score:  One of the better product shots I''ve seen so far.  The reliance on ''water drop'' to boost a generic offering, however, is really getting old for me. Sadly, that''s my own peeve, as I''m sure it''s going nowhere.', '2010-04-30 17:07:29.000000', NULL, 1);
